A||||1||dman||Batboy, info please on some rims you've mentioned||||5||
Z||000000||dman||04-27-2000||07:41 PM||||Hi Batboy,<P>In response to two seperate posts (both a few weeks back), you mentioned that the DRW wheels may be a good low cost rim for the Fiero. <P>One of your previous posts can be found at:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/003167.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/003167.html</A> <P>The DRW rims can be viewed at:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.wheelsone.com/drw_wheels.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.wheelsone.com/drw_wheels.asp</A> <P>I might be interested in the 870 model. I was wondering if you know (with confidence) if that rim will actually fit, with the proper offset as well as bolt pattern.<P>The 870 comes in 17x7 as well as 16x7. I'd probably go with the 16 inch rim. The prices range from $70 a piece (16x7 silver) to $110 (17x7 chrome).<P>Any info you have on this would be greatly appreciated.<P>BTW, if anyone else knows of a good set of 16inch rims that will definitely fit a fiero, at a good price (no more than $120 please), please post as well.<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||04-27-2000||11:08 PM||||I'm assuming you'll need to contact Wheels One and find out if they'll fit. You'll need 5 lug holes by 100mm wheels. I personally have not looked into them yet, I spent my Batmobile wheel and tire budget on my truck's 454 engine.||||reg||1
